BRepFill_Sweep: reverse a ring pcurve only for opposite directions

When BRepFill_Sweep attaches the parameter curve of a closed ring edge
(the section circle shared by two consecutive swept faces) to a face, it
decides whether to reverse the curve by comparing the ring's 3D tangent
with the surface direction against an angular tolerance of 1e-4 rad.
That is a test for "not parallel", not for "opposite": any tangent
discontinuity of the spine above 0.0057 deg that reaches this code
without a corner treatment (RightCorner below the angmin gate, or the
Transformed mode which never treats corners) mirrors the parameter
curve, and BRepCheck reports InvalidCurveOnSurface and
InvalidSameParameterFlag on the ring. Meshing such a face produces a
band of inverted triangles between the two rings.

Only reverse when the directions are opposite.

